MiaUI modifications vs upstream cobaltgit/Butterscotch (pinned at
92ed6b8c3766361a201a69d202bcde5873cdad7e):

- patches/001-rg35xx-fallback-mapping.patch (new): createFallbackMappings()
  for the RG35XX gpio-keys pad (dpad at sdl 13-16, volume key at 12)
- patches/002-chunklog.patch, patches/003-stage-markers.patch,
  patches/004-sdl-error.patch, patches/005-sdl1-error.patch,
  patches/006-fpslog.patch: diagnostics (chunk/stage/FPSLOG markers,
  SDL_GetError() in init failures)
- patches/007-joyname-cache.patch: cache SDL_JoystickName() per slot
  (SDL 1.2 opens the device + issues ioctls every call; ~50ms/frame)
- patches/008-exit-cursor.patch: Select+Start clean-exit combo, hide the
  fbcon stub cursor
- Dockerfile retargeted to arm-buildroot-linux-gnueabihf (glibc 2.37,
  INTERP /lib/ld-linux-armhf.so.3), SDL1.2 fbcon + ALSA, software renderer
- launch.sh: ROMs/Ports/Undertale.pak/ layout, SDL_VIDEODRIVER=fbcon,
  SDL_NOMOUSE=1, CPU governor pinning, debug.log probe

Upstream code retains its own licenses; see upstream/LICENSE (AGPLv3).
Upstream is vendored under upstream/ and is re-cloneable at the pinned
commit (see .gitignore).

